--! A test platform's one capability: make every later `child_process.spawn`
--! give a child that starts, says what its standard input is, and whose
--! input pipe fails with an error code of the caller's choosing, by the
--! route Node takes for a write that failed. It reaches what
--! `ChildProcess.run` asks of Node for the standard input, and what it does
--! with an error of the input pipe, with no real pipe and no race.

--| From now on, every `child_process.spawn` gives a child that starts. A
--| child whose standard input is a pipe fails its first write with an
--| error whose `code` is the given one. After that, or at once when it has
--| no pipe, the child writes what `spawn` was asked for as its standard
--| input (`pipe`, `ignore`) and exits 0.
pub foreign impure failInput : String → ⊤
